course: dictionary
lesson: 5750
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, so you must check the clues around it. The word lover is a good example. «She is a nature lover, so she spends every weekend in the woods.» The clues nature and the woods tell you a lover is someone who really enjoys something.
explain: A lover of something is a person who likes it very much. «Dad is a chocolate lover, so he always buys the biggest bar.» Chocolate lover means a person who likes chocolate very much. Try the meaning in the sentence instead of the hard word. Does it still make sense? If it does, you have probably got it right.
explain: Some words are friendly greetings in one place and mean nothing special in another. «Alright my lover» is said in the West Country of England, around Bristol, to anyone. It is a friendly word, like "dear" or "mate". When the clues are not enough, ask a local friend or look in a dictionary.
fact: A lover of something is a person who likes it very much, such as an animal lover or a book lover.
fact: «Dog lover» means a person who really likes dogs.
fact: In stories and poems, young lovers can mean two people who love each other, as in Romeo and Juliet.
fact: In the West Country of England, «my lover» is a friendly word, said to anyone, like "dear".
fact: The same word can mean different things, so always read the words around it to find its meaning.
exercise: «She is a nature lover, so she spends every weekend in the woods.» What does lover mean here? | A person who lives in the woods | A person who works for a zoo | A person who is sad about nature | *A person who likes nature very much
exercise: «Dad is a chocolate lover, so he always buys the biggest bar.» What is a chocolate lover? | *A person who likes chocolate very much | A person who makes chocolate in a factory | A person who has never tasted chocolate | A person who sells sweets in a shop
exercise: In the West Country, a man says «Alright my lover» to a stranger. What does it mean? | A warning to stay away | A rude way to tell someone to go away | A question about their family | *A friendly greeting, like "dear" or "mate"
test: What does a book lover like? | *Reading books | Sleeping late | Running very fast | Cooking dinner
test: «Romeo and Juliet» is a famous play about young lovers. What are young lovers? | Two people who are always angry | Two people who never meet | *Two people who love each other | Two people who work together
exam: In Bristol, «my lover» is said to anyone. What does this tell you about the word? | It is a rude word | *It is a friendly, everyday greeting | It is the name of a town | It can only be used for animals
